; Not steps after the first: a count reads the whole state.  Under step every
; over a set store, done's match reads (p 1), which is there from the start,
; but its count of (q 2) holds only once grow has made (q 2).  Meeting only the
; matches that read a fresh row would never fire done, so this program's steps
; meet every match.
(store set)
(step every)
(p 1)
(rule grow (read (p $x)) (make (q 2)))
(rule done (read (p $x)) (count 1 (q 2)) (make (done $x)))
